1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,398
At Bayer, every new business question tends to become a new dashboard.

2
00:00:05,398 --> 00:00:10,296
The result is hundreds of reports, conflicting KPI definitions, reports nobody owns,

3
00:00:10,296 --> 00:00:12,337
and a growing maintenance bill.

4
00:00:12,737 --> 00:00:15,186
Reuse Gate sits before the build.

5
00:00:15,186 --> 00:00:20,084
It checks the existing reports first, and recommends reuse, repair, extension, migration,

6
00:00:20,084 --> 00:00:24,573
or a new build, with every decision backed by cited data.

7
00:00:24,573 --> 00:00:26,206
A person always approves.

8
00:00:26,606 --> 00:00:31,504
Here, a business user asks for a Nubeqa sales dashboard in plain

9
00:00:31,504 --> 00:00:32,704
words.

10
00:00:32,704 --> 00:00:37,602
Reuse Gate asks what is unclear, then answers on one card: don't

11
00:00:37,602 --> 00:00:38,802
build.

12
00:00:38,802 --> 00:00:43,700
Extend an existing report that already covers two of the three KPIs.

13
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:48,998
The analyst sees every row behind that answer, and can turn it

14
00:00:48,998 --> 00:00:53,488
into a dashboard preview filled with real rows from the data.

15
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:58,786
For a new oncology build, the gates block release because the data

16
00:00:58,786 --> 00:01:00,418
model's owner is inactive.

17
00:01:00,418 --> 00:01:05,316
The approver simulates one active owner, all seven gates pass, and the

18
00:01:05,316 --> 00:01:09,398
decision is recorded with an owner and a review date.

19
00:01:09,798 --> 00:01:14,696
A developer proposes a rule change, and it is measured on all

20
00:01:14,696 --> 00:01:18,778
one hundred and fifty requests before anyone may approve it.

21
00:01:19,178 --> 00:01:24,076
Every role has its own view and sees only its own data.

22
00:01:24,476 --> 00:01:29,373
On Bayer's synthetic data pack, fifty-seven of one hundred and fifty requests

23
00:01:29,373 --> 00:01:31,006
avoid a new build.

24
00:01:31,006 --> 00:01:35,088
That is thirty-eight percent fewer dashboards to build and maintain.

25
00:01:35,088 --> 00:01:38,353
One owner fix would unblock eighty more specs.

26
00:01:38,353 --> 00:01:40,802
These figures are modelled, not measured.

27
00:01:41,202 --> 00:01:44,876
All of this runs on Red Hat OpenShift AI.

28
00:01:44,876 --> 00:01:49,773
The decision service is deployed as a model with KServe, and it

29
00:01:49,773 --> 00:01:53,039
shows up here, in the OpenShift AI dashboard.

30
00:01:53,039 --> 00:01:56,304
The app shows each decision ran on KServe.

31
00:01:56,304 --> 00:02:01,202
Before every release, an OpenShift Pipelines run checks the tests and the

32
00:02:01,202 --> 00:02:03,243
governance, evaluation, and security gates.

33
00:02:03,243 --> 00:02:08,141
The decisions are rules, not guesses, so they are repeatable and auditable.

34
00:02:08,141 --> 00:02:09,341
Build less.

35
00:02:09,341 --> 00:02:10,541
Build better.

